#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run SqDRIFT to generate CI strings {#run-sqdrift-to-generate-ci-strings}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you already ran `./SqDRIFT` through Steps 1–4, `alphadets_from_sqd.txt` "
"already exists in the project root and you can skip this step. Otherwise, "
"run it from the project root:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run the diagonalization {#run-the-diagonalization}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Parameters:**\n"
"- `--fcidump`: Path to the FCIDump file containing the Hamiltonian\n"
"- `--adetfile`: Path to the alpha determinants file (CI strings from SqDRIFT)\n"
"- `--method 0`: Davidson diagonalization method\n"
"- `--iteration 100`: Maximum number of Davidson iterations\n"
"- `--block 10`: Block size for Davidson algorithm\n"
"- `--tolerance 1e-8`: Convergence tolerance for energy\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Energy = -107.5108722590187` line is the ground-state estimate over the"
" sampled subspace.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How this differs from the Python example {#how-this-differs-from-the-python-"
"example}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The two examples differ in several respects at once, not only in how they "
"treat bad-symmetry bitstrings, so they are not expected to produce identical"
" energies:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | C++ tab | Python tab |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| Bad-symmetry bitstrings | **Discarded** by `postselect_bitstrings` on Hamming weight | **Repaired** by iterative configuration recovery |\n"
"| Loop structure | Single pass: sample → postselect → diagonalize once | Outer loop: diagonalize, read orbital occupancies, recover configurations, re-diagonalize |\n"
"| Circuit count | 100 circuits (`num_circuits = 100`) | 400 circuits (200 per evolution time) |\n"
"| Evolution times | A single $\\tau$ (`time_step = 1`) | Two times, `times = [1.0, 10.0]` |\n"
"| Diagonal terms | Kept in the sampled operator | Removed by `filter_diagonal_terms`, changing the sampling distribution and the circuits |\n"
"| Term ordering | Grouped only | `canonical_order` applied before grouping for reproducibility |\n"
"| Diagonalization solver | **SBD** (`diag`, external MPI/OpenMP binary) | `qiskit-addon-sqd` in-process solver |\n"
"| Backend | Fixed by name (`backend_name = \"ibm_fez\"`; the run on this page used `ibm_pittsburgh`) | `least_busy` operational backend with enough qubits |\n"
"| Transpilation | Each circuit separately, optimization level 2 | All circuits together, optimization level 3 |\n"
"| Job submission | 100 jobs, one circuit each | One Sampler job containing all 400 circuits |\n"
"| Simulator run | None; hardware only | Noiseless simulator example before the hardware run |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both versions use the same Hamiltonian, group its terms by electronic "
"structure, weight each group by the mean absolute coefficient of its terms, "
"start from the Hartree-Fock state, and sample 10 groups and 100 shots per "
"circuit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each difference affects the sampled subspace, and therefore the energy, "
"independently. The larger ensemble and the second, longer evolution time "
"both broaden the configurations the Python example explores; sampling at "
"more than one time gives SqDRIFT its Krylov-like coverage of the low-energy "
"space. Filtering diagonal terms changes which operators the sampler can draw"
" and their weights, so the two runs sample different distributions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Postselection is a strict filter, and a shot with the wrong particle number "
"is dropped outright. In the run above that discarded most of the data, 1137 "
"of 10000 shots survived the (7,7) Hamming-weight check (about 11%), "
"collapsing into just 49 distinct $\\alpha$-determinants. Configuration "
"recovery instead uses average orbital occupancies from a prior "
"diagonalization to flip bits and *repair* such shots, recycling what "
"postselection would discard. That feedback makes it inherently iterative: "
"`recover_configurations` in `qiskit-addon-sqd-hpc` requires an "
"`avg_occupancies` argument that exists only after a diagonalization has "
"run.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This C++ run yields a subspace of 49 $\\alpha$-determinants and an energy of"
" `-107.5109` Ha. The full $\\alpha$-determinant space for seven electrons in"
" 10 orbitals is only $\\binom{10}{7} = 120$ strings, so feeding all 120 to "
"the same `diag` binary gives the exact FCI energy `-107.6482` Ha. The run "
"therefore sits about `0.1373` Ha above exact while spanning 49 of the 120 "
"$\\alpha$-determinants. Since SQD is variational in the selected subspace, a"
" smaller subspace can only raise the energy, so the incomplete subspace is "
"the most direct reading of the gap.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This exact-FCI check is only possible because the example is small; it is "
"not part of the SqDRIFT workflow, and for system sizes where SQD is actually"
" needed, no such reference exists. It serves here only to quantify how much "
"of the space this run recovered.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A comparison against the Python example is not controlled, so a difference "
"should not be attributed to the absence of configuration recovery alone; "
"note that circuit count, the single evolution time, diagonal-term filtering,"
" and hardware noise all differ at once and all shape the subspace.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To close the gap, here are some possible next steps to try after completing "
"this tutorial: raise `shots`, `num_circuits`, or `ops_per_circuit`; sample "
"at more than one `time_step`; and add a recovery loop on top of "
"`Qiskit::addon::sqd::recover_configurations`.\n"
msgstr ""

